    <string name="setup_title">Setting up Quest Shelf</string>
    <string name="setup_intro">Quest Shelf needs two things switched on in the headset\'s settings. Each row below opens the right screen; come back here afterwards.</string>
    <string name="setup_go">Open</string>
    <string name="setup_service">Open instead of Meta\'s library</string>
    <string name="setup_service_on">On. Quest Shelf opens on the menu button and after the headset starts.</string>
    <string name="setup_service_off">Off. Until it is on, Quest Shelf is just one more app in the library.</string>
    <string name="setup_service_hint">In the list that opens, find “%s” and switch it on. Android will warn that the service can see what is on screen: Quest Shelf only looks at which window is in front.</string>
    <string name="setup_restricted">The switch is greyed out?</string>
    <string name="setup_restricted_sub">Open the app\'s page, then the ⋮ menu, then “Allow restricted settings”, and try again.</string>
    <string name="setup_usage">Play statistics</string>
    <string name="setup_usage_on">Allowed. “Last played”, play time and the running game work.</string>
    <string name="setup_usage_off">Not allowed. In the list that opens, find Quest Shelf and allow it.</string>
    <string name="setup_net_note">To get a cover, Quest Shelf asks the OculusDB service (and a spare source on GitHub) for it by the game\'s package name, title or store id. Nothing about you or your account is sent.</string>
    <string name="setup_no_screen">This headset has no such screen. See the README for the way with a computer.</string>
